        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 24 at 3:45PM AKDT until September 25 at 5:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK</headline>
        <description>Coastal Waters Forecast for the Northern Gulf of Alaska Coast
up to 100 nm out including Kodiak Island and Cook Inlet.

Wind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction
expected. Sea forecasts represent an average of the highest
one-third of the combined wind wave and swell height.

.TONIGHT...E wind 25 kt. Seas 2 ft building to 4 ft by midnight.
.FRI...E wind 30 kt. Seas 5 ft. Rain showers.
.FRI NIGHT...E wind 15 kt. Seas 2 ft. Rain showers.
.SAT...SE wind 15 kt. Seas 2 ft.
.SAT NIGHT...SE wind 10 kt. Seas 2 ft.
.SUN...E wind 10 kt. Seas 2 ft.
.MON THROUGH TUE...Variable wind less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft.
</description>
